{
  "esm": "0.7.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WRF_hourly_d01_loader",
    "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for WRF regional weather fields from the UCAR Research Data Archive dataset d340000 (WRF-Chem v3.9.1, CONUS domain, 12 km grid). Supplies hourly meteorological 3-D fields (wind components, potential temperature, pressure, geopotential, water vapor) on the native Lambert Conformal Conic (LCC) Arakawa-C grid.\n\nThis is the loader half of the wrf loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.1). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template), the file variables it reads (with units), its temporal cadence, and its NATIVE grid expressed as a GDD Grid with a PROJECTED (lambert_conformal) crs descriptor carrying the LCC projection parameters. It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding — those are concerns of the regridding model (components/earthsci_data/wrf.esm), which references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./wrf_loader.esm\"}.\n\nThe removed co-located blocks: the old DataLoaderSpatial block (proj4 crs string / grid_type / staggering / resolution / extent) is replaced by the GDD `grid` (family + crs{projection:lambert_conformal, datum:sphere, R, parameters} + dimensions + extents); the old per-loader `regridding` block (fill_value / extrapolation) is gone — regridding is declared per-variable on the model (wrf.esm `regrid`). Because a `temporal` block is present, this loader seeds DISCRETE cadence (ess-v9a.5): the runtime refreshes the file buffers hourly.\n\nThe LCC projection parameters {lat_1:30, lat_2:60, lat_0:38.999996, lon_0:-97, R:6370000} match the WRF grid and are consumed by the downstream reprojection rule (ESD reprojection/lambert_conformal.esm, esd-47z.2) and the ESD projected-grid construction (discretizations/grids/lambert_conformal/wrf_lcc.esm, esd-47z.5).\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/wrf.jl:169 (WRFFileSet). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/wrf.esm (esm-4l84).",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "meteorology",
      "atmospheric_dynamics",
      "data_loader",
      "regional_climate",
      "wrf",
      "conus",
      "lambert_conformal",
      "pure-io"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciData.jl contributors",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.1)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Skamarock, W. C., Klemp, J. B., Dudhia, J., Gill, D. O., Liu, Z., Berner, J., Wang, W., Powers, J. G., Duda, M. G., Barker, D. M., and Huang, X.-Y. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR Tech. Note NCAR/TN-556+STR, doi:10.5065/1dfh-6p97.",
        "url": "https://www2.mmm.ucar.edu/wrf/users/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "UCAR Research Data Archive, dataset d340000. WRF-Chem v3.9.1 CONUS 12 km hourly output, May 2019 – May 2026. https://rda.ucar.edu/datasets/d340000/",
        "url": "https://rda.ucar.edu/datasets/d340000/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/wrf.jl:169 (WRFFileSet struct, WRF constructor)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "data_loaders": {
    "WRF_hourly_d01": {
      "kind": "grid",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "https://data.rda.ucar.edu/d340000/{date:%Y%m}/wrfout_hourly_d01_{date:%Y-%m-%d}_{date:%H}:00:00.nc"
      },
      "temporal": {
        "start": "2019-05-01T00:00:00Z",
        "end": "2026-05-31T23:59:59Z",
        "file_period": "PT1H",
        "frequency": "PT1H",
        "records_per_file": 1,
        "time_variable": "Times"
      },
      "grid": {
        "family": "cartesian",
        "crs": {
          "projection": "lambert_conformal",
          "datum": "sphere",
          "R": 6370000.0,
          "parameters": {
            "lat_1": 30.0,
            "lat_2": 60.0,
            "lat_0": 38.999996,
            "lon_0": -97.0
          }
        },
        "description": "Native WRF grid: Lambert Conformal Conic projection on an Arakawa C-grid, CONUS domain at 12 km horizontal resolution. The crs descriptor carries the spherical LCC parameters (standard parallels 30°/60°, origin 38.999996°N/-97°E, sphere radius 6370000 m) consumed by the regridding model's reprojection (ESD reprojection/lambert_conformal.esm, esd-47z.2). Migrated from the loader's former DataLoaderSpatial block (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1); the loader describes this grid but performs no reprojection or regridding. Mass (cell-centered) dimensions west_east/south_north/bottom_top hold scalars (T, P, PB, QVAPOR); the staggered (cell-edge) dimensions west_east_stag/south_north_stag/bottom_top_stag hold the C-grid wind/geopotential fields (U on west_east_stag, V on south_north_stag, W/PH/PHB on bottom_top_stag). Dimension cell counts are resolved from the source dataset at load time; the documented d01 mass-grid geometry is 389 × 229 × 32 (west_east × south_north × bottom_top).",
        "dimensions": [
          "west_east",
          "south_north",
          "bottom_top",
          "west_east_stag",
          "south_north_stag",
          "bottom_top_stag"
        ],
        "extents": {
          "west_east": {
            "n": 389,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "south_north": {
            "n": 229,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "bottom_top": {
            "n": 32,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "west_east_stag": {
            "n": 390,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "south_north_stag": {
            "n": 230,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "bottom_top_stag": {
            "n": 33,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "U": {
          "file_variable": "U",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Zonal (west–east) wind component. WRF output variable U on the west_east_stag grid (C-grid x-edges). The regridding model interpolates this staggered field with a B-spline kernel."
        },
        "V": {
          "file_variable": "V",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Meridional (south–north) wind component. WRF output variable V on the south_north_stag grid (C-grid y-edges). The regridding model interpolates this staggered field with a B-spline kernel."
        },
        "W": {
          "file_variable": "W",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Vertical wind component. WRF output variable W on the bottom_top_stag grid (C-grid z-edges). The regridding model interpolates this staggered field with a B-spline kernel. Zero extrapolation below the surface (extrapolate_type=0.0 in the upstream loader, overriding the default clamp for this variable only)."
        },
        "T": {
          "file_variable": "T",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Perturbation potential temperature (K). On the mass (bottom_top) grid, cell-centred. Full potential temperature θ = T + 300 K."
        },
        "PH": {
          "file_variable": "PH",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "description": "Perturbation geopotential (m² s⁻²). On the w-level (bottom_top_stag) grid. Together with PHB provides geopotential height z = (PH+PHB)/g."
        },
        "PHB": {
          "file_variable": "PHB",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "description": "Base-state geopotential (m² s⁻²). On the w-level (bottom_top_stag) grid. Together with PH provides geopotential height z = (PH+PHB)/g."
        },
        "P": {
          "file_variable": "P",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Perturbation pressure (Pa). On the mass (bottom_top) grid, cell-centred. Together with PB provides total atmospheric pressure P_total = P + PB."
        },
        "PB": {
          "file_variable": "PB",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Base-state pressure (Pa). On the mass (bottom_top) grid, cell-centred. Together with P provides total atmospheric pressure P_total = P + PB."
        },
        "QVAPOR": {
          "file_variable": "QVAPOR",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Water vapor mixing ratio (kg water kg⁻¹ dry air). On the mass (bottom_top) grid, cell-centred."
        }
      },
      "reference": {
        "citation": "UCAR Research Data Archive, dataset d340000. WRF-Chem v3.9.1 CONUS 12 km hourly output.",
        "url": "https://rda.ucar.edu/datasets/d340000/"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "wrf",
          "meteorology",
          "regional_climate",
          "conus",
          "lambert_conformal",
          "12km"
        ],
        "earthscidata_source": "src/wrf.jl::WRFFileSet",
        "domain_id": "d01",
        "projection": "lambert_conformal_conic",
        "map_proj": 1,
        "lcc_parameters": {
          "truelat1": 30.0,
          "truelat2": 60.0,
          "cen_lat": 38.999996,
          "stand_lon": -97.0,
          "sphere_radius_m": 6370000.0
        },
        "native_resolution_m": {
          "west_east": 12000.0,
          "south_north": 12000.0
        },
        "native_extent_m": {
          "west_east": [-2334000.0, 2334000.0],
          "south_north": [-1374000.0, 1374000.0]
        },
        "mass_grid_dimensions": [389, 229, 32],
        "model_version": "WRF-Chem v3.9.1",
        "proj4_string": "+proj=lcc +lat_1=30.0 +lat_2=60.0 +lat_0=38.999996 +lon_0=-97.0 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +a=6370000 +b=6370000 +to_meter=1",
        "wrf_variable_note": "The upstream WRF() constructor reads ALL variables in the WRF output file dynamically via WRFFileSet.varnames(). This loader documents the nine core meteorological variables (U, V, W, T, PH, PHB, P, PB, QVAPOR) present in all CONUS d340000 files and that drive EarthSciML coupling. Additional WRF-Chem tracer/diagnostic variables (T2, U10, V10, PSFC, chemistry species) can be added as additional loader variables.",
        "staggering_note": "WRF uses an Arakawa C-grid. Staggered-grid variables (U on west_east_stag, V on south_north_stag, W/PH/PHB on bottom_top_stag) live on the cell-edge dimensions; scalars (T, P, PB, QVAPOR) live on the mass (cell-centred) dimensions. The regridding model (wrf.esm) regrids the C-grid wind components U/V/W with a B-spline interpolating kernel and the scalars conservatively (RFC §5.2). The upstream EarthSciData.jl loader de-staggers staggered variables to cell centres in loadmetadata; the GDD grid above preserves the native staggered dimensions so the regridding model can choose the kernel by location.",
        "access_note": "UCAR RDA data access requires a free registration at https://rda.ucar.edu/. The upstream EarthSciData.jl WRFFileSet uses standard HTTP downloads (login cookie only). Ensure $EARTHSCIDATADIR is set for local caching.",
        "w_extrapolation_note": "Vertical wind W uses zero-boundary extrapolation (extrapolate_type=0.0) in the upstream loader to prevent spurious mass transport through the ground surface. All other variables use clamp extrapolation. Per-variable extrapolation override is a future ESM-schema concern; here it is documented for the runtime."
      }
    }
  }
}
